  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - Botswana Global Procurement Initiative Training and Orientation Visit, through Business Council for International Understanding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Global Procurement Initiative activity trained officials from the Republic of Botswanas Public Procurement and Asset Disposal Board (PPADB) on how to incorporate best-value determination into public procurements by utilizing objective evaluation methods such as life-cycling cost analysis. In Phase I, officials received procurement training in Botswana in March 2014. In Phase II, procurement officials from Botswana traveled to the United States in December 2014 for an orientation visit that included follow-on training and meetings. As the PPADB and relevant Ministries incorporate best-value determination and life-cycle costing into their procurement processes on a regular basis, this may increase international competition in public tenders and may help level the playing field for U.S. companies.</narrative>
  </description>
